BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The MGT Million Celebration and Bike Ride
DTSTART:20261205T190000Z
DTEND:20261205T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20261127T054227Z
UID:b4a73890-444d-528a-933b-6ba2f1523ef5
DESCRIPTION:Bundle up\, grab your bike helmet or walking shoes\, and join 
 us at the water’s edge in anticipation of the millionth rider to roll on
  the Martin Goodman Trail (MGT) since the bike counter was installed at Lo
 wer Simcoe in May.\n\nThe (https://www.instagram.com/bicyclemayorto/) Bicy
 cle Mayor of Toronto and (https://www.instagram.com/bikesauceto/) Bike Sau
 ce will be leading a 6 km slow roll on the MGT\, ending at Sherbourne Comm
 on. View the (https://ridewithgps.com/routes/57773954) 6km route.\n\nThe (
 https://www.waterfrontbia.com/) WaterfrontBIA will be providing hot bevera
 ges and refreshments.\n\n* 1:45 pm - registration begins for folks borrowi
 ng Bike Share bikes* (on a first come first serve basis)\n* 2:00 pm gather
  at the (https://maps.app.goo.gl/RCCDh48bxrUkE9Au9) Bike Share station loc
 ated between Rees St and Simcoe (near the wavedeck on the waterfront)\n* 2
 :15 pm - Welcome remarks and overview of the route and safe group riding t
 ips\n* 3:00 pm - Arrive at Sherbourne Common overlooking Lake Ontario for 
 hot beverages\, light refreshments\, arts and crafts\, bike checks\, and l
 ively social gathering.\n* 4:30 pm - event ends\n\n(https://bikesharetoron
 to.com/) Bike Share Toronto* will be providing bikes (on a first come firs
 t serve basis).\n\n(https://www.cycleto.ca/) Cycle Toronto will be providi
 ng bike checks and lights.\n\nThe (https://www.instagram.com/to_cycling_pe
 d/) City of Toronto’s Cycling & Pedestrian Projects Unit will bring bike
  maps and a wealth of information about biking in Toronto year round.\n\n(
 https://www.instagram.com/femmesandfriendsbike/) Femmes and Friends will h
 ave arts and crafts for people to express their love for Toronto's bike la
 nes.\n\nBike Share bikes are available on a first come\, first serve basis
 . *Participants must register and sign their waiver.\n\nImportant Informat
 ion:\n\nNote: if you’re bringing your own bike\, all participants must h
 ave working lights and a bell. We encourage all participants to wear a hel
 met\; however\, they are mandatory (and the law) for people 16 years and u
 nder\, and for those riding e-bikes.\n\nDress for the weather. Bring water
  and good vibes.\n\nThis event is designed to welcome anyone identifying a
 s a human\, regardless of modal preferences\, sexual orientation\, gender
 \, income\, race or religion. Children are welcome and must be accompanied
  by a parent or guardian. By your participation in this event\, you agree 
 to be respectful of others and will contribute to building a comfortable a
 nd inclusive environment where everyone feels welcome.\n\nThe organizers r
 eserve the right to remove any participant who is deemed to be disrespectf
 ul\, disruptive\, or deemed to pose a threat to themselves or others.\n\nD
 isclaimer:\n\nWhile the safety of participants will be prioritized\, every
  rider is responsible for their own actions\, decisions\, and well-being. 
 Riders are expected to follow the rules of the road\, ride defensively\, s
 tay alert to any hazards\, bike safely at all times\, and listen to direct
 ion provided by the ride leaders. Bicycling\, as with any activity conduct
 ed over public pavements and facilities comes with risk.\n\nBy participati
 ng in this ride hosted by the Bicycle Mayor of Toronto and Bike Sauce\, yo
 u acknowledge and agree that you will be riding at your own risk. The Bicy
 cle Mayor\, along with its ride leaders and organizers\, do not assume res
 ponsibility for any injury\, loss\, damage\, or incident that may occur be
 fore\, during\, or after the ride\, and does not assume a duty of care for
  participants. You further agree and warrant that if\, at any time\, you b
 elieve conditions to be unsafe\, you will immediately discontinue further 
 participation\, and will let the organizers know prior to departing.\nURL:
  https://www.cycleto.ca/the_mgt_million_celebration_and_bike_ride
LOCATION:Simcoe WaveDeck\n243 X Queens Quay West\nToronto ON M5J 2G8\nCA
URL:https://www.cycleto.ca/the_mgt_million_celebration_and_bike_ride
END:VEVENT
